      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "These results using herpes virus-mediated gene transfer to overexpress enkephalin in the amygdala support the role of amygdalar opioids in the anxiolytic actions of benzodiazepines and supraspinal nociception (see ref. 1). These studies also demonstrate the usefulness of recombinant herpes virus in evaluating the role of single gene products within specific brain sites in pharmacological responses and complex behaviors."},
